        "text": "Jacob bought a bunch of violets from Nell and asked her, kindly, whether she saw anyone near Carrow’s warehouse the morning he died.\n\nNell took the coin, tucked it into her apron, and gave the flowers a small shake to settle the petals. “Aye, I did,” she said, her voice low enough that the passing costermongers would not catch it. “Just before the sky went grey. A young fellow slipped out the side door of the warehouse. Clerk’s coat, neat as you like, carrying a small leather case. He looked about once, sharp-like, then walked quick toward Whitechapel High Street. I thought it odd at the time, but with the market opening I let it go.”\n\nShe met Jacob’s eyes for a moment, guarded but steady. “That’s all I saw, sir. Nothing more.”\n\nThe gas lamps along the market edge still burned low in the damp morning air.",
